{
  "id": "pc-circles",
  "chapterNumber": "2",
  "title": {
    "en": "Unit Circle & Trigonometric Identities",
    "ar": null
  },
  "content": {
    "blocks": [
      {
        "kind": "text",
        "body": {
          "en": "The unit circle extends trigonometry to all real numbers. Trigonometric identities are equations true for all values of the variable — they allow simplification, equation solving, and calculus manipulations.",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "def",
        "label": {
          "en": "● Unit circle and periodicity",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "<p>For angle \\(\\theta\\) in standard position, terminal point on unit circle: \\((\\cos\\theta,\\sin\\theta).\\)</p>\\[\\sin(\\theta+2\\pi)=\\sin\\theta,\\quad\\cos(\\theta+2\\pi)=\\cos\\theta,\\quad\\tan(\\theta+\\pi)=\\tan\\theta.\\]<p><strong>Even/Odd:</strong> \\(\\cos(-\\theta)=\\cos\\theta\\) (even); \\(\\sin(-\\theta)=-\\sin\\theta\\) (odd); \\(\\tan(-\\theta)=-\\tan\\theta\\) (odd).</p>",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "thm",
        "label": {
          "en": "● Fundamental identities",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "\\[\\sin^2\\theta+\\cos^2\\theta=1,\\quad1+\\tan^2\\theta=\\sec^2\\theta,\\quad1+\\cot^2\\theta=\\csc^2\\theta.\\]\\[\\tan\\theta=\\frac{\\sin\\theta}{\\cos\\theta},\\quad\\cot\\theta=\\frac{\\cos\\theta}{\\sin\\theta}.\\]",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "explorer",
        "title": {
          "en": "⊙ Explorer · The unit circle",
          "ar": null
        },
        "canvasId": "ucCanvas",
        "ariaLabel": {
          "en": "A point moving around the unit circle, with its projections onto the axes showing cosine and sine",
          "ar": null
        },
        "dataPanel": {
          "btnId": "ucDataBtn",
          "panelId": "ucDataPanel",
          "descId": "ucDataDesc",
          "rowsId": "ucDataRows",
          "caption": {
            "en": "The current point's coordinates and trig ratios",
            "ar": null
          },
          "columns": [
            {
              "en": "quantity",
              "ar": null
            },
            {
              "en": "value",
              "ar": null
            }
          ]
        },
        "controls": [
          {
            "id": "ucT",
            "valueDisplayId": "ucTlab",
            "label": {
              "en": "angle <b>θ</b>:",
              "ar": null
            },
            "ariaLabel": {
              "en": "Angle theta",
              "ar": null
            },
            "min": 0,
            "max": 360,
            "value": 40,
            "step": 1
          }
        ],
        "readouts": [
          {
            "id": "ucCos",
            "label": {
              "en": "cos θ",
              "ar": null
            },
            "colorClass": "indigo"
          },
          {
            "id": "ucSin",
            "label": {
              "en": "sin θ",
              "ar": null
            },
            "colorClass": "amber"
          },
          {
            "id": "ucTan",
            "label": {
              "en": "tan θ",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "id": "ucQuad",
            "label": {
              "en": "quadrant",
              "ar": null
            }
          }
        ],
        "note": {
          "en": "The point \\(P=(\\cos\\theta,\\sin\\theta)\\) always lies on \\(x^2+y^2=1\\) — that's exactly the Pythagorean identity \\(\\sin^2\\theta+\\cos^2\\theta=1\\) above.",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "thm",
        "label": {
          "en": "● Sum & difference formulas",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "\\[\\sin(A\\pm B)=\\sin A\\cos B\\pm\\cos A\\sin B,\\]\\[\\cos(A\\pm B)=\\cos A\\cos B\\mp\\sin A\\sin B,\\]\\[\\tan(A\\pm B)=\\frac{\\tan A\\pm\\tan B}{1\\mp\\tan A\\tan B}.\\]",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "thm",
        "label": {
          "en": "● Double-angle & half-angle formulas",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "\\[\\sin2\\theta=2\\sin\\theta\\cos\\theta,\\]\\[\\cos2\\theta=\\cos^2\\theta-\\sin^2\\theta=1-2\\sin^2\\theta=2\\cos^2\\theta-1,\\]\\[\\tan2\\theta=\\frac{2\\tan\\theta}{1-\\tan^2\\theta}.\\]\\[\\sin\\frac{\\theta}{2}=\\pm\\sqrt{\\frac{1-\\cos\\theta}{2}},\\quad\\cos\\frac{\\theta}{2}=\\pm\\sqrt{\\frac{1+\\cos\\theta}{2}},\\quad\\tan\\frac{\\theta}{2}=\\frac{1-\\cos\\theta}{\\sin\\theta}.\\]",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "def",
        "label": {
          "en": "● Product-to-sum & sum-to-product formulas",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "\\[\\sin A\\cos B=\\tfrac{1}{2}[\\sin(A+B)+\\sin(A-B)],\\]\\[\\cos A\\cos B=\\tfrac{1}{2}[\\cos(A-B)+\\cos(A+B)],\\]\\[\\sin A+\\sin B=2\\sin\\!\\left(\\frac{A+B}{2}\\right)\\cos\\!\\left(\\frac{A-B}{2}\\right).\\]",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "workedExampleCard",
        "label": {
          "en": "Worked Example 2.1 — Exact value",
          "ar": null
        },
        "problem": {
          "en": "Find the exact value of \\(\\cos(75°)\\).",
          "ar": null
        },
        "solution": {
          "en": "<p>\\(\\cos75°=\\cos(45°+30°)=\\cos45°\\cos30°-\\sin45°\\sin30°\\)</p><p>\\(=\\dfrac{\\sqrt2}{2}\\cdot\\dfrac{\\sqrt3}{2}-\\dfrac{\\sqrt2}{2}\\cdot\\dfrac{1}{2}=\\dfrac{\\sqrt6-\\sqrt2}{4}.\\)</p>",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "workedExampleCard",
        "label": {
          "en": "Worked Example 2.2 — Identity proof",
          "ar": null
        },
        "problem": {
          "en": "Prove: \\(\\dfrac{\\sin2\\theta}{1+\\cos2\\theta}=\\tan\\theta.\\)",
          "ar": null
        },
        "solution": {
          "en": "<p>LHS: \\(\\dfrac{2\\sin\\theta\\cos\\theta}{1+(2\\cos^2\\theta-1)}=\\dfrac{2\\sin\\theta\\cos\\theta}{2\\cos^2\\theta}=\\dfrac{\\sin\\theta}{\\cos\\theta}=\\tan\\theta=\\) RHS. \\(\\checkmark\\)</p>",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "workedExampleCard",
        "label": {
          "en": "Worked Example 2.3 — Solve trig equation",
          "ar": null
        },
        "problem": {
          "en": "Solve \\(\\cos2\\theta+\\cos\\theta=0\\) on \\([0°,360°)\\).",
          "ar": null
        },
        "solution": {
          "en": "<p>Replace \\(\\cos2\\theta=2\\cos^2\\theta-1\\): \\(2\\cos^2\\theta-1+\\cos\\theta=0.\\)</p><p>Factor: \\((2\\cos\\theta-1)(\\cos\\theta+1)=0.\\)</p><p>\\(\\cos\\theta=\\frac{1}{2}\\Rightarrow\\theta=60°,300°.\\quad\\cos\\theta=-1\\Rightarrow\\theta=180°.\\)</p>",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "workedExampleCard",
        "label": {
          "en": "Worked Example 2.4 — Given value, find related",
          "ar": null
        },
        "problem": {
          "en": "If \\(\\sin\\theta=\\frac{5}{13}\\) and \\(\\theta\\) is in Q2, find \\(\\sin2\\theta\\) and \\(\\cos\\frac{\\theta}{2}.\\)",
          "ar": null
        },
        "solution": {
          "en": "<p>Q2: \\(\\cos\\theta=-\\frac{12}{13}.\\quad\\sin2\\theta=2\\sin\\theta\\cos\\theta=2\\!\\left(\\frac{5}{13}\\right)\\!\\left(-\\frac{12}{13}\\right)=-\\frac{120}{169}.\\)</p><p>\\(\\cos\\frac{\\theta}{2}=+\\sqrt{\\frac{1+\\cos\\theta}{2}}=\\sqrt{\\frac{1-12/13}{2}}=\\sqrt{\\frac{1/13}{2}}=\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{26}}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{26}}.\\) (Q2 \\(\\Rightarrow\\theta/2\\in\\) Q1, so cosine positive.)</p>",
          "ar": null
        }
      }
    ]
  },
  "quizWidget": {
    "enabled": true
  }
}
